# Intent is SELF-HOSTED on v3. Inside this checkout, `intent` must be the v3
# binary -- otherwise the shipped v2 CLI at ~/.local/bin/intent (PATH 17) wins
# and you silently test the wrong product. That shadowing is invisible: v2
# answers `--version` happily and reports 2.19.0 from inside the rewrite.
#
# Scoped deliberately to this directory tree. The fleet's `intent` is v2 and
# must stay v2 -- fifteen projects depend on it -- so this must never be a
# machine-wide PATH change.
#
# SIDE EFFECT, AND IT IS A WANTED ONE: with v3 first, `intent info` reports
# INTENT_HOME as this checkout, so the pre-commit guard bodies resolve from
# lib/templates/hooks/ HERE (tracked, versioned with the repo) instead of from
# the frozen Intentv2 checkout. That is the drift exposure closed for Intent,
# and it is the same tracked-in-repo shape Lamplight already uses.
PATH_add "$(expand_path native/rust/target/debug)"
